# Platform Migration (read first)

This repo is migrating from a single React Router app to a workspace:
`apps/web` (this code) · `apps/core-api` (new private backend) · `apps/integration-api` (public customer API).

**Current work: `docs/stage-1-tasks.md`** — ordered, dependency-aware checklist. The #4 deploy gate has passed: `apps/core-api` runs on Azure Container Apps and reaches production in about 3 ms. #6 is done: the shared `resolvePerson` / `recordPersonEvent` writers live in `apps/core-api/src/lib/`. Next is #7, the `people` API slice.

Stage 0 is complete and archived in `docs/stage-0-tasks.md` — workspace, `apps/web`, `apps/integration-api`, `@luhive/db`, CI.

**The query layer is Kysely.** Hand-written SQL migrations, the database is the source of truth, types are generated from it. Workflow in `packages/db/README.md`; never edit generated type files or an applied migration.

**The spec is authoritative.** It is symlinked into this repo:

- `docs/spec-moc.md` — decisions, stages, live risks. Start here.
- `docs/spec/` — 17 numbered documents. `04` structure, `05` conventions, `05a` a full worked example, `15` stages and gates.

Read the relevant spec document before proposing architecture, and follow it over any assumption from the existing code.

## Scope of the other rules

The naming rule, `.cursor/rules/core/naming.mdc`, applies to handwritten code across **all apps and shared packages**.

All remaining rules in `.cursor/rules/**`, except this migration rule, describe **`apps/web` only** — the existing React Router app. Those web-specific rules do not govern `apps/core-api` or `apps/integration-api`, which follow `docs/spec/04` and `docs/spec/05` instead (vertical slices, Hono, services, `Result<T>`, Kysely).

Do not "fix" new backend code to match the web app's module/repo layout.

## Standing constraints during migration

- **`app/modules/events/**` is frozen.** Bug fixes only, no refactors, no restructuring. See `docs/spec/12`.
- **Cleanup is only authorised on the path to a slice being migrated.** Do not refactor files you were not already changing.
- **Business logic moves to `apps/core-api`, not sideways.** New rules never get added to `apps/web` server actions.
- Never introduce new RLS policies. Tenant scoping lives in application code.
